<h1 id=3D"IIQSailpointIntegration-Processflow">Process flow&nbsp;</h1>
<p><strong>User Creation</strong></p>
<ol>
 <li>Through IIQ, SAAs to set up the employee with CompassX access as requi=
red (Coarse grained access)</li>
 <li>IIQ to sync the user details to OKTA&nbsp;</li>
 <li>IIQ to invoke FUM's API (#2) to sync the user to CX also&nbsp;</li>
 <li>SAAs to use FUM UI to further define Fine-grained access of the user&n=
bsp;</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>User Updates</strong></p>
<ol>
 <li>Through IIQ, SAAs to modify the user details/access (Coarse grained ac=
cess)</li>
 <li>IIQ to sync the details to OKTA&nbsp;</li>
 <li>IIQ to invoke FUM's API (#3) to sync the user details to CX also&nbsp;=
</li>
 <li>FUM to review the Fine-grained access of the user based on the new IIQ=
 access and override existing access if required.&nbsp;</li>
 <li>SAAs to use FUM UI to further define Fine-grained access of the user&n=
bsp;</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Disabling Users</strong></p>
<ol>
 <li>IIQ to receive events whenever an employee is terminated/removed.&nbsp=
;</li>
 <li>IIQ to sync the details to OKTA&nbsp;</li>
 <li>IIQ to invoke FUM's API (#3) to sync the user details to CX also with =
active flag as 'false'</li>
 <li>FUM to set the user status as disabled in CX also</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Overnight Jobs</strong></p>
<ol>
 <li>IIQ to use FUM's user details API (#4) to get the list of all employee=
s with the latest access. This will ensure access to match between IIQ and =
FUM.&nbsp;=20
  <ol>
   <li>Only internal users (employees) to be part of this list&nbsp;</li>
  </ol></li>
 <li>IIQ to use FUM's userAccess API (#5) to get the list of all possible u=
serAccess and reflect the same in IIQ</li>
</ol>
<h1 id=3D"IIQSailpointIntegration-Appendix">Appendix</h1>
<h2 id=3D"IIQSailpointIntegration-OpenQuestions">Open Questions</h2>
<ol>
 <li>Need to discuss with business on the access group and how these access=
 groups should be mapped ibn FUM. like=20
  <ol>
   <li>
    <div class=3D"table-wrap">
     <table class=3D"wrapped confluenceTable">
      <tbody>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Access Group In IIQ</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">CX Access (FUM)</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">CX Modules</td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td rowspan=3D"2" class=3D"confluenceTd">Trading</td>
        <td rowspan=3D"2" class=3D"confluenceTd">View ??</td>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Trading</td>
       </tr>
       <tr>
        <td class=3D"confluenceTd">Mutual Funds</td>
       </tr>
      </tbody>
     </table>
    </div></li>
  </ol></li>
</ol>
<p>&nbsp; &nbsp;<time datetime=3D"2025-11-26" class=3D"date-past">26 Nov 20=
25</time> Decided to use compassX access group as <strong>CompassX&nbsp;</s=
trong>which will provide just basic level of access to CX until security ad=
visor provide more fine grained access.&nbsp;</p>
<ol>
 <li>Employee Tenant migration of existing employees from external to inter=
nal.&nbsp;</li>
</ol>
